{"timestamp":1774905298922,"source_app":"agentic-harness","session_id":"20aeeaa9-44ec-451e-8211-fa3aa71a8408","hook_event_type":"PreToolUse","tool_name":"Read","tool_use_id":"toolu_01TdnGKHwcfAY4HtMCFhPPE7","payload":{"session_id":"20aeeaa9-44ec-451e-8211-fa3aa71a8408","transcript_path":"/Users/rivero/.claude/projects/-Users-rivero-ai-agentic-experience-apps-mas-trees-9ee16026/20aeeaa9-44ec-451e-8211-fa3aa71a8408.jsonl","cwd":"/Users/rivero/ai/agentic-experience/apps/mas/trees/9ee16026","permission_mode":"bypassPermissions","hook_event_name":"PreToolUse","tool_name":"Read","tool_input":{"file_path":"/Users/rivero/ai/agentic-experience/apps/mas/trees/9ee16026/studio/src/mas-repository.js","offset":200,"limit":30},"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TdnGKHwcfAY4HtMCFhPPE7"}}
{"timestamp":1774905343224,"source_app":"agentic-harness","session_id":"20aeeaa9-44ec-451e-8211-fa3aa71a8408","hook_event_type":"PreToolUse","tool_name":"Write","tool_use_id":"toolu_01VwtkF6xpEtjbD6gG7L8CDD","payload":{"session_id":"20aeeaa9-44ec-451e-8211-fa3aa71a8408","transcript_path":"/Users/rivero/.claude/projects/-Users-rivero-ai-agentic-experience-apps-mas-trees-9ee16026/20aeeaa9-44ec-451e-8211-fa3aa71a8408.jsonl","cwd":"/Users/rivero/ai/agentic-experience/apps/mas/trees/9ee16026","permission_mode":"bypassPermissions","hook_event_name":"PreToolUse","tool_name":"Write","tool_input":{"file_path":"/Users/rivero/ai/agentic-experience/apps/mas/trees/9ee16026/.pinata/specs/issue-11-adw-9ee16026-sdlc_planner-prevent-duplicate-fragment-title-clone.md","content":"# Plan: Prevent Duplicate Fragment Title for Cloned Cards in M@S Studio\n\n## Summary\nWhen a card is cloned in M@S Studio, the new fragment inherits the same Fragment Title as the original because `titleClone` is initialized to `''` and only updated if the user types in the dialog. The fix initializes `titleClone` to the fragment's current title on dialog open and, in `copyFragment()`, auto-generates a unique title by appending a `-N` numeric suffix when the proposed title already exists among fragments in the same parent folder path.\n\n## Task Description\nIntroduce a uniqueness check for Fragment Title scoped to the parent folder path when a card is cloned:\n- Initialize `titleClone` to `this.fragment.title` when the clone dialog opens (both `editor-panel.js` and `mas-fragment-editor.js`).\n- Add a pure utility function `generateUniqueFragmentTitle(baseTitle, existingTitles)` that increments a `-N` suffix until the title is unique.\n- In `copyFragment()` in `mas-repository.js`, after the AEM copy returns, collect existing fragment titles from the in-memory store scoped to the same parent folder path and resolve a unique title before saving.\n- Add unit tests for `generateUniqueFragmentTitle`.\n\n## Relevant Files\n\n| File | Action | Reason |\n|------|--------|--------|\n| `studio/src/utils/fragment-utils.js` | **Create** | New utility: `generateUniqueFragmentTitle` |\n| `studio/src/mas-repository.js` | **Edit** | Apply unique-title logic in `copyFragment()` |\n| `studio/src/editor-panel.js` | **Edit** | Initialize `titleClone` in `showClone()` |\n| `studio/src/mas-fragment-editor.js` | **Edit** | Initialize `titleClone` in `showClone()` |\n| `studio/test/fragment-utils.test.js` | **Create** | Unit tests for `generateUniqueFragmentTitle` |\n\n## Step by Step Tasks\n\n### 1. Create `studio/src/utils/fragment-utils.js` with `generateUniqueFragmentTitle`\n\nAdd a pure utility function that accepts a base title and a set/array of existing titles, and returns a title guaranteed to be absent from the set:\n\n```js\n/**\n * Returns a title unique among existingTitles.\n * If baseTitle already exists, appends -1, -2, \u2026 until unique.\n * If baseTitle ends with -N, strips the suffix before incrementing\n * so that successive clones produce -1, -2, -3 (not -1-1, -1-2).\n *\n * @param {string} baseTitle\n * @param {string[]} existingTitles\n * @returns {string}\n */\nexport function generateUniqueFragmentTitle(baseTitle, existingTitles) {\n    const titleSet = new Set(existingTitles);\n    if (!titleSet.has(baseTitle)) return baseTitle;\n\n    const match = baseTitle.match(/^(.*)-(\\d+)$/);\n    const stem = match ? match[1] : baseTitle;\n    let counter = 1;\n    while (titleSet.has(`${stem}-${counter}`)) counter++;\n    return `${stem}-${counter}`;\n}\n```\n\n### 2. Edit `studio/src/mas-repository.js` \u2014 apply deduplication in `copyFragment()`\n\n- Import `generateUniqueFragmentTitle` at the top of the file.\n- Inside `copyFragment(updatedTitle, osi, tags)`, after `const result = await this.aem.sites.cf.fragments.copy(this.fragmentInEdit)`:\n  1. Determine the base title: `updatedTitle || result.title`.\n  2. Derive the parent folder path from `result.path` by splitting on `/` and dropping the last segment.\n  3. Collect existing titles from `Store.fragments.list.data` where the fragment's path starts with the same parent folder path. Exclude the newly created copy itself (by `result.id`).\n  4. Call `generateUniqueFragmentTitle(baseTitle, existingTitles)` to get the final title.\n  5. If the resolved title differs from `result.title`, set `result.title = resolvedTitle` and ensure `needsSave = true`.\n\nRevised logic sketch (replace lines 1017\u20131027):\n```js\nconst parentPath = result.path.split('/').slice(0, -1).join('/');\nconst existingTitles = Store.fragments.list.data\n    .get()\n    .filter((s) => {\n        const f = s.get();\n        return f && f.id !== result.id && f.path.startsWith(parentPath + '/');\n    })\n    .map((s) => s.get().title);\n\nconst baseTitle = updatedTitle || result.title;\nconst resolvedTitle = generateUniqueFragmentTitle(baseTitle, existingTitles);\nconst needsSave = resolvedTitle !== result.title || osi;\nif (needsSave) {\n    if (resolvedTitle !== result.title) result.title = resolvedTitle;\n    result.fields.forEach((field) => {\n        if (osi && field.name === 'osi') field.values = [osi];\n    });\n    savedResult = await this.aem.sites.cf.fragments.save(result);\n}\n```\n\n### 3. Edit `studio/src/editor-panel.js` \u2014 initialize `titleClone` in `showClone()`\n\nIn the `showClone()` method (around line 620), add:\n```js\nthis.titleClone = this.fragment.title;\n```\nbefore `this.showCloneDialog = true;`.\n\n### 4. Edit `studio/src/mas-fragment-editor.js` \u2014 initialize `titleClone` in `showClone()`\n\nSame change in the `showClone()` method (around line 1088):\n```js\nthis.titleClone = this.fragment.title;\n```\nbefore `this.showCloneDialog = true;`.\n\n### 5. Create `studio/test/fragment-utils.test.js` \u2014 unit tests\n\n```js\nimport { expect } from '@esm-bundle/chai';\nimport { generateUniqueFragmentTitle } from '../src/utils/fragment-utils.js';\n\ndescribe('generateUniqueFragmentTitle', () => {\n    it('returns baseTitle unchanged when no conflict', () => {\n        expect(generateUniqueFragmentTitle('card-a', ['card-b'])).to.equal('card-a');\n    });\n    it('appends -1 for first conflict', () => {\n        expect(generateUniqueFragmentTitle('lucy-card', ['lucy-card'])).to.equal('lucy-card-1');\n    });\n    it('increments suffix past existing clones', () => {\n        expect(generateUniqueFragmentTitle('lucy-card', ['lucy-card', 'lucy-card-1'])).to.equal('lucy-card-2');\n    });\n    it('strips existing -N suffix before incrementing', () => {\n        expect(generateUniqueFragmentTitle('lucy-card-1', ['lucy-card-1'])).to.equal('lucy-card-2');\n    });\n    it('handles empty existingTitles', () => {\n        expect(generateUniqueFragmentTitle('card', [])).to.equal('card');\n    });\n    it('skips gaps (e.g. -1 taken, -2 free)', () => {\n        expect(generateUniqueFragmentTitle('card', ['card', 'card-1', 'card-2'])).to.equal('card-3');\n    });\n});\n```\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Cloning a card whose Fragment Title already exists in the same folder produces a new title with a `-1` suffix.\n- Cloning a card whose title ends in `-N` produces `-N+1` (no double-suffix like `-1-1`).\n- Multiple successive clones in the same folder yield `-1`, `-2`, `-3`, etc.\n- The original card's Fragment Title is not modified.\n- Manual title edits in the clone dialog are respected (the uniqueness check uses the user's typed title as the base, not the original).\n- No two cards in the same parent folder share the same Fragment Title after a clone operation.\n\n## Validation Commands\n\n- `node --check studio/src/utils/fragment-utils.js`\n- `node --check studio/src/mas-repository.js`\n- `node --check studio/src/editor-panel.js`\n- `node --check studio/src/mas-fragment-editor.js`\n- `node --check studio/test/fragment-utils.test.js`\n"},"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VwtkF6xpEtjbD6gG7L8CDD"}}
